============================================================================
READING 1 -- TURNS PER HUBBLE TIME, WHICH FALLS WITH TEMPERATURE
============================================================================
  at T_sph:  theta_dot/H = 2.4e+06  ->  3.820e+05 turns per Hubble time

     T/T_sph    T (with T_sph = 130 GeV)    turns per Hubble
  ------------------------------------------------------------
    1.00e+00                     130 GeV           3.820e+05
    1.00e-03                     130 MeV           3.820e+02
    1.31e-05                     1.7 MeV           5.004e+00
    1.00e-08                     1.3 keV           3.820e-03
    2.00e-12     0.26 eV (recombination)           7.639e-07

  the five-turn threshold branch (a) needs is crossed at T/T_sph = 1.309e-05,
  i.e. T = 1.70 MeV on a 130 GeV sphaleron shutoff.
  Below that the instantaneous winding is too slow for equidistribution, and by
  recombination it is 7.6e-07 turns per Hubble time -- entirely frozen.

============================================================================
READING 2 -- TOTAL ACCUMULATED TURNS, WHICH SATURATES
============================================================================
  theta_dot dt = (theta_dot/H)_sph . dT/T_sph, so the accumulated winding from T_sph
  down to T is (theta_dot/H)_sph . (1 - T/T_sph) radians -- flat in T, hence dominated
  by the earliest epoch and saturating almost immediately.

   down to T/T_sph    accumulated turns   % of the total
  --------------------------------------------------------
             5e-01           1.9099e+05            50.0%
             1e-01           3.4377e+05            90.0%
             1e-02           3.7815e+05            99.0%
             1e-04           3.8193e+05           100.0%
             0e+00           3.8197e+05           100.0%

  total accumulated winding below T_sph: 3.820e+05 turns

============================================================================
WHAT EACH READING DOES TO f_bar, AND SO TO BRANCH (a)
============================================================================
  on the ACCUMULATED reading, N = 3.82e+05 turns:
    worst-case deviation of f_bar from 2/pi  ~ 2.64e-05%
    against the 2.08% branch (a) needs  ->  the route is DEAD by six orders

  on the INSTANTANEOUS reading the answer depends entirely on the epoch that sets
  epsilon: above ~1.7 MeV the premise holds, below it the phase is frozen and
  f_bar is not an average at all but whatever value the phase happens to sit at.

  So the two readings do not merely differ in precision, they differ in kind, and
  nothing recorded says which one the epsilon-assembly uses. That is the owed piece:
  not 'is equidistribution granted' but 'over what window is the average taken'.
  Under the accumulated reading -- the natural one for a phase that has been winding
  since genesis -- f_bar is pinned and the alpha_c conflict stands at its full 2.08%.
